hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16816","Abd Allah said: Abu Musa al-Anazi narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: Sakan ibn al-Mughira narrated to me, he said: al-Walid ibn Abi Hisham narrated to me from Farqad Abu Talha from Abd al-Rahman ibn Khabbab al-Sulami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and urged contributions for the army of hardship, and Uthman ibn Affan said: Upon me are one hundred camels with their saddles and their packs. He said: Then he urged, and Uthman said: Upon me are another one hundred with their saddles and their packs. He said: Then he came down a step of the minbar, then he urged, and Uthman ibn Affan said: Upon me are another one hundred with their saddles and their packs. He said: And I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying with his hand like this, moving it, and Abd al-Samad brought out his hand as one amazed: Whatever Uthman does after this, no harm shall be upon him."
"16817","Abd Allah said: Abu Musa al-Anazi narrated to me, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Sakan ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Hisham narrated to us from Abu Talha from Abd al-Rahman ibn Khabbab al-Sulami, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching and urging contributions for the army of hardship, and he mentioned it."
